  "headnotes": [
    {
      "la": "…emens cedit injuriae [n: (Gen. XXIX, 18-28)]. Quorsum autem ista? Ut et tu si jam sponsa Christi es, ardeas amore, aestues desiderio, anheles suspiriis, dum tardat dies copulae concupitae. Ait quidam,",
      "en": "… what end these things? That you too, if you are already the bride of Christ, may burn with love, seethe with desire, pant with sighs, while the day of the longed-for union delays. A certain man says,",
      "column": "1044b",
      "chunk": 0
    },
    {
      "la": "…rescit! [n: (Isa. LI.)] Libet inter haec meminisse, quod sanctus Germanus pontifex Antissiodorensis Romam petens, cum Aeduam devenisset, ad tumulum sancti Cassiani divertit; quem proprio vocans nomine",
      "en": "…I.)] It is pleasant here to recall that holy Germanus, bishop of Auxerre, on his way to Rome, when he had come to Autun, turned aside to the tomb of holy Cassian; and calling him by his own name, said",
      "column": "1046a",
      "chunk": 0
    },
    {
      "la": "Et ille de tumulo -",
      "en": "And he from the tomb",
      "column": "1046a",
      "chunk": 0
    }
